gcc-14 14.2.0-19 / clang-19 19.1.7:
  CC -std=gnu11 -march=armv8-a+crypto -O{0,2} arm-neon-polynomial-long.c -o probe
  All four builds and executions exit 0, no program output.
The source checks 36 operand pairs including bit 63, all-ones and asymmetric
values, both 64-bit result halves, high-lane selection and once-only operands.
RED: no Rust build errors; C-HIR first reports E3007 at the poly128 object
declaration, exposing its missing nominal scalar storage classification.
GREEN: C-HIR and EvoIR return 0; assembly is emitted using existing wide
integer instructions, with no new instruction or external-call substitution.
The emitted assembly is independently linked by both fixed compilers and
both native executions return 0. Original object acceptance is a separate gate.
Reference: https://arm-software.github.io/acle/neon_intrinsics/advsimd.html
